"""The HTTP transport, and the only package in this service that may import
FastAPI. `make lint` fails the build if any other package does.

It nests one level deeper than it needs to — `internal/transport/http` rather
than `internal/http` — so that a second transport is a peer directory and not
a refactor. Do not flatten it. See `docs/architecture.md`.

Belongs here: routing, request decoding, response encoding, the mapping from
an error category to an HTTP status, middleware, and the server's own
timeouts.

Does NOT belong here: business rules, validation beyond "is this the shape I
was promised", or anything that reads a database. Handlers call the service
layer with plain Python values and serialize what comes back.
"""
